NAME
       errno - the last error

SYNOPSIS
       #include <errno.h>

DESCRIPTION
       Set by a failing library or system call. It is only meaningful
       after a call that reported failure, and is not cleared by one
       that succeeded, so test the return value first.

COMMON VALUES
       ENOENT   no such file or directory
       EACCES   permission denied
       EEXIST   the file already exists
       EBADF    bad file descriptor
       ENOTDIR  a path component is not a directory
       EISDIR   the target is a directory
       ENOMEM   out of memory
       EINVAL   invalid argument
       EAGAIN   the operation would block
       EINTR    interrupted by a signal
       ENODEV   no such device
       EPERM    operation not permitted
       ENOSPC   no space left on device
       EXDEV    cross-device link

SEE ALSO
       open(2), read(2), poll(2)
